{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"argv": ["git", "commit", "-q", "-m", "F044 and D056: correct the four summaries that carried the count, and record what the counting changed\n\nThe population is 20 rows rather than twelve, and prior art is a plurality with a\none-row margin rather than a majority. STATE.md, HYPOTHESES.md,\nSTATE-next-actions.md and FAILURES-findings-6.md all stated the twelve; each now\nstates what was measured, and FAILURES-findings-6's own headline is corrected\nin place because F026's conclusion survives on the narrower evidence.\n\nThe second reading matters more than the first: 7 of the 18 died of something\nelse -- a mechanism its own test refuted or confirmed into uselessness, a claim no\nobservation could establish, or a promotion with no gate priced. Item 0 gains\nthat option with a count behind it, and keeps its owner-decision status.\n\nSTATE-in-flight-2.md holds the closed readings item 0 leans on, split from\nSTATE-in-flight.md at the cap. classify.py splits into rowcheck.py (does the\nrecord obey its own rule) and the gates, with every figure identical across the\nsplit."], "cwd": "/home/ubuntu/think-free", "duration_ms": 175, "exit_code": 0, "log": "sessions/2026-10-05-010-test-whether-twelve-candidates-twelve-pr/commands.log", "log_line_end": 98, "log_line_start": 91, "redactions": [], "summary": "$ git commit -q -m F044 and D056: correct the four summaries that carried the count, and record what the counting changed\n\nThe population is 2"}, "duration_ms": 175, "exit_code": 0, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "command", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 16, "session": "2026-10-05-010-test-whether-twelve-candidates-twelve-pr", "ts": "2026-10-05T13:51:28+00:00"}
